<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RM_Miasma                                      MIASMA_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 - Phase A
    Phase A row 19 of design/RimMandrake/biome_mod_architecture.md. Parent:
    BIOME_MOD_SPLIT_EXECUTION_1. Governed by BIOME_PAINT_ONCE_AT_THE_END_1 - this
    def is expected to carry 0 tiles until the terminal repaint; that is not a
    defect.

    Copied from the frozen src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_Miasma.xml
    (kept, unchanged except a header comment, still carrying the live campaign
    world's painted tiles). This is a NEW, franchise-free sibling for any other
    generated RimWorld planet, not a rename of that one.

    RM tier: nothing here knows what campaign or planet uses it. Fully donor-free
    for wildlife would be nice but is NOT true today - see the wildAnimals/wildPlants
    notes below, matching the honesty standard every sibling RM_ biome mod ships
    (compare RM_PoisonForest's own About.xml "NOT entirely donor-free" section).

    workerClass: replaces the donor AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_MiasmicMangrove with
    this mod's own RM_BiomeWorker_Miasma (RM_MiasmaBiome.cs) - a donor type in
    workerClass is a hard dependency the RimMandrake tier may not assume
    (biome_mod_architecture.md Sec5 step 2).

    wildAnimals: 14 rows ship inline -
      - 9 non-Star-Wars donor rows (Alpha Animals / VFE Insectoids 2), each already
        MayRequire-gated on its own donor mod, unchanged from the twin (Q9).
      - RUT_Karrobel / RUT_Karrathil, this campaign's own invented (non-canon,
        franchise-free) delta-loam composter and fever-swarm vector - these two
        ThingDefs still physically live in mandrake.rut.patches (not moved this
        pass, out of MIASMA_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 SS6's scope), so they carry a fresh
        MayRequire="mandrake.rut.patches" here that the twin's own copy never
        needed (same-mod, no gate required there). A future pass can port them
        into this mod outright (they are invented names, RM tier per Q11a) and
        drop the gate.
      - RM_Karravel / RM_Karrimeth / RM_Karrolun (MIASMA_FAUNA_FLOOR_ROSTER_1):
        the arthropod floor's other three scuttlers, native to this mod from the
        start since it already exists (unlike when Karrobel/Karrathil shipped).
        All four scuttlers share one population pool via
        RM_VerminPressureExtension's "RM_MiasmaScuttlers" group tag - see
        RM_Miasma_ArthropodFloor.xml and the retrofit on RUT_Karrobel.xml.
    The 15 genuine Star Wars rows the twin also carries do NOT ship here - they
    ride Utinni's WildAnimals_Miasma.xml as a PatchOperationAdd onto this def,
    MayRequire-gated per row's real source mod, per the Q11a naming-tier ruling.
    Two more of the twin's rows (RSW_RustNipperJuv/RSW_SiltLampreyJuv) were
    ALSO on that patch until SEA_BEASTS_TIER_RULING_1 (2026-09-25) found their
    parents (rust nipper, silt lamprey) are INVENTED, not canon - they ship
    inline above instead, as RM_RustNipperJuv/RM_SiltLampreyJuv.
    The 5 rows the roster itself evicted (Kreetle, Yobshrimp, RSW_Gembug,
    AA_BloodShrimp, AA_Plasmorph - see rosters/the_miasma.json's own evictions[])
    are dropped outright, not carried forward into either mod.

    wildPlants: MIASMA_FLORA_ROSTER_1 replaced the three donor Alpha Biomes
    mangal rows (AB_MangroveTree/AB_ParasiticMangrove/AB_MangrovePalm,
    sarg.alphabiomes, 96.5% of this biome's flora weight) with the roster's
    own four RM_-tier mangals (RM_Thessamor/RM_Brelloch/RM_Quennath/
    RM_Ilbareen, src/RimMandrake/Miasma/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/
    RM_Miasma_Mangals.xml) and added the roster's other 15 invented rows
    (six rainbow blooms, five predators, four muck-and-silt plants) - see
    that same folder's RM_Miasma_RainbowBlooms.xml/RM_Miasma_Predators.xml/
    RM_Miasma_MuckAndSilt.xml. mandrake.rm.miasma now depends on ZERO donor
    flora and needs no sarg.alphabiomes MayRequire on any wildPlants row.
    RUT_Nogtyl (mandrake.rut.rotsporekit) is left exactly as the twin has
    it - THEROT_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 owns updating that MayRequire when Nogtyl's
    home mod is renamed, not this item. RM_IlbareenDead is a 20th plant def
    that never appears in this list - see the RM_GradientAxisExtension
    landRepaintKillPlant/landRepaintDeadPlant fields below.

    terrainsByFertility: AB_FertileMud gains the same MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes"
    guard for the same reason.

    biomeMapConditions / modExtensions: unchanged in shape from the twin. The
    GameConditionDef/HediffDef/IncidentDef/WeatherDef/ThingDef/GenStepDef/
    Patch content they reference (16 files) moved into this mod's own Defs/ and
    Patches/ trees with their defNames UNCHANGED - nothing here needed to be
    retargeted, since the frozen twin references the exact same defNames and
    both mods are expected to load together going forward. The two onlyInBiomes/
    allowedBiomes lists inside that moved content (the breath-tide surge
    incident, the seven ForgeOnSurvival disease patches) now name BOTH
    RUT_Miasma and RM_Miasma, so the mechanics keep firing on the live save.

    texture (Biomes/AB_MiasmicMangrove) is inherited unchanged from the twin,
    same posture as RM_PoisonForest's own donor world-map texture - not this
    build's scope to fix.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RM_Miasma</defName>
    <label>the Miasma</label>
    <description>A salt-crusted, stilt-rooted mangal forest standing in brackish channels between a dying sea and the rivers that feed it, under a green-gold haze of its own breath. Walking is hard, the air hangs thick, and the water crowds with life -- because everything ends up here: the water, the sins it carries, and the life running from the salt. Threaded through the stink, improbably, beauty: rainbow-hued plants, young animals everywhere, and the stubborn sense the place is on the verge of something.</description>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.Miasma.RM_BiomeWorker_Miasma</workerClass>
    <foragedFood>RawBerries</foragedFood>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>6.5</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.7</plantDensity>
    <forageability>1.0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>4</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>Biomes/AB_MiasmicMangrove</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>15</diseaseMtbDays>
    <biomeMapConditions>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock</li>
    </biomeMapConditions>
    <modExtensions>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards" Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.BiomeGlowMultiplierExtension">
        <glowMultiplier>0.85</glowMultiplier>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards" Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GradientAxisExtension">
        <waterBands>
          <li>
            <max>0.34</max>
          </li>
          <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.flowworks">
            <max>0.66</max>
            <terrainShallow>RM_WaterBrackishShallow</terrainShallow>
            <terrainDeep>RM_WaterBrackishDeep</terrainDeep>
          </li>
          <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.flowworks">
            <max>1</max>
            <terrainShallow>RM_WaterBrineShallow</terrainShallow>
            <terrainDeep>RM_WaterBrineDeep</terrainDeep>
          </li>
        </waterBands>
        <landRepaintMinSalinity>0.85</landRepaintMinSalinity>
        <landRepaintSource>
          <li>Mud</li>
          <li MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">AB_FertileMud</li>
        </landRepaintSource>
        <landTerrain>RUT_Jawa_SaltCrust</landTerrain>
        <!-- MIASMA_FLORA_ROSTER_1: the salt-line gauge. The moment a cell
             holding a living RM_Ilbareen repaints to landTerrain (brine has
             just reached it), RM_GradientAxisRepaint kills it and spawns
             RM_IlbareenDead in its place — a real, self-maintaining record
             of the last surge's reach, not decoration. -->
        <landRepaintKillPlant>RM_Ilbareen</landRepaintKillPlant>
        <landRepaintDeadPlant>RM_IlbareenDead</landRepaintDeadPlant>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards" Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GradientSurgeExtension">
        <incidentDef>RUT_Surge</incidentDef>
        <baseMtbDays>5</baseMtbDays>
        <stormMtbMultiplier>0.25</stormMtbMultiplier>
        <stormWindSpeedThreshold>1.2</stormWindSpeedThreshold>
        <frontCellsRange>15~35</frontCellsRange>
        <recedeDaysRange>2~4</recedeDaysRange>
        <residualFraction>0.15</residualFraction>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards" Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_StrandingPoolsExtension">
        <!-- SEA_BEASTS_TIER_RULING_1 (2026-09-25): RSW_SiltLampreyJuv's parent
             (silt lamprey) is one of the roster's 11 INVENTED sea beasts, so
             this row moved to the RM_ tier (RM_SeaBeasts_Invented.xml,
             mandrake.rm.terminalbiomes). RSW_MeeJuv/RSW_YobshrimpJuv's
             parents (mee scalefish, pale yobshrimp) are genuine canon and
             stay RSW_. -->
        <strandedSpawnList>
          <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_MeeJuv</li>
          <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_YobshrimpJuv</li>
          <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.terminalbiomes">RM_SiltLampreyJuv</li>
        </strandedSpawnList>
        <emptyWeight>40</emptyWeight>
        <smallWeight>50</smallWeight>
        <bigWeight>10</bigWeight>
        <strandedCountSmall>1~2</strandedCountSmall>
        <strandedCountBig>3~5</strandedCountBig>
        <decayDaysRange>3~8</decayDaysRange>
        <poolSizeThreshold>4</poolSizeThreshold>
        <searchRadius>60</searchRadius>
        <dryTerrain>RUT_Jawa_SaltCrust</dryTerrain>
        <strandedDeformationHediff>RUT_StrandedDeformation</strandedDeformationHediff>
        <strandedDeformationChance>0.25</strandedDeformationChance>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <diseases>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">
        <diseaseInc>AB_Disease_BacterialGangrene</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">
        <diseaseInc>AB_Disease_ViralAbasia</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">
        <diseaseInc>AB_Disease_RavagingIntestinalParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Malaria</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>160</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SleepingSickness</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>140</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Mud</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.65</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">AB_FertileMud</terrain>
        <min>0.65</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>8</Clear>
      <Fog>5</Fog>
      <Rain>10</Rain>
      <DryThunderstorm>0.9</DryThunderstorm>
      <RainyThunderstorm>5</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>4</FoggyRain>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <RUT_Karrobel MayRequire="mandrake.rut.patches">0.6</RUT_Karrobel>  <!-- karrobel - delta-loam composter, this campaign's own invented species, still authored in mandrake.rut.patches -->
      <RUT_Karrathil MayRequire="mandrake.rut.patches">0.9</RUT_Karrathil>  <!-- karrathil - fever-swarm vector/pollinator, same as above -->
      <!-- SEA_BEASTS_TIER_RULING_1 (2026-09-25): two of the Miasma nursery's seven
           juveniles whose parents are INVENTED sea beasts, not genuine Star Wars IP
           (verified via Wookieepedia's search API: no canon hit for either name) —
           moved off the mandrake.rsw.swbestiary-gated WildAnimals_Miasma.xml patch
           and shipped here instead, so a franchise-free install still gets a real
           nursery. Parent adults (RM_RustNipper/RM_SiltLamprey) live in
           mandrake.rm.terminalbiomes (RM_SeaBeasts_Invented.xml). -->
      <RM_RustNipperJuv MayRequire="mandrake.rm.terminalbiomes">0.25</RM_RustNipperJuv>
      <RM_SiltLampreyJuv MayRequire="mandrake.rm.terminalbiomes">0.25</RM_SiltLampreyJuv>
      <!-- MIASMA_FAUNA_FLOOR_ROSTER_1 - the other three arthropod-floor scuttlers, native RM_ tier -->
      <RM_Karravel>3.5</RM_Karravel>  <!-- karravel - the carpet; the bulk of the floor, cheap protein for everything -->
      <RM_Karrimeth>0.8</RM_Karrimeth>  <!-- karrimeth - the mass; an event, not background, wildGroupSize carries the "carpet crossing" read -->
      <RM_Karrolun>1.2</RM_Karrolun>  <!-- karrolun - the harvest; the arthropod industry's actual target -->
      <VFEI2_Swarmling MayRequire="oskarpotocki.vfe.insectoid2">0.7</VFEI2_Swarmling>  <!-- swarmlings - vermin -->
      <VFEI2_BlackSwarmling MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.5</VFEI2_BlackSwarmling>  <!-- black swarmlings - vermin -->
      <AA_Lockjaw MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.2</AA_Lockjaw>  <!-- lockjaw - channel-predator -->
      <AA_Mantrap MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.2</AA_Mantrap>  <!-- mantrap - root-ambush -->
      <AA_RaptorShrimp MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.2</AA_RaptorShrimp>  <!-- raptor shrimp - channel-predator -->
      <AA_DecayDrake MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_DecayDrake>  <!-- decay drake - composter -->
      <AA_Helixien MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Helixien>  <!-- helixien - strange -->
      <AA_Slurrypede MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Slurrypede>  <!-- slurrypede - composter -->
      <AA_Thermadon MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Thermadon>  <!-- thermadon - channel-predator -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <!-- MIASMA_FLORA_ROSTER_1 - the four mangals (roster §3), replacing the donor trio -->
      <RM_Thessamor>9</RM_Thessamor>  <!-- thessamor - the stilt-root maze itself -->
      <RM_Brelloch>6</RM_Brelloch>  <!-- brelloch - the seaward salt-line marker -->
      <RM_Quennath>3</RM_Quennath>  <!-- quennath - the parasite that never touches brine -->
      <RM_Ilbareen>4</RM_Ilbareen>  <!-- ilbareen - the salt-line gauge; dies to RM_IlbareenDead, see landRepaintKillPlant above -->
      <!-- the six rainbow blooms (roster §4), all bound by ban 2 - never a trap, never toxic -->
      <RM_Ollamane>6</RM_Ollamane>  <!-- ollamane - the biome's signature fan silhouette -->
      <RM_Vellamine>2</RM_Vellamine>  <!-- vellamine - colour along the veins -->
      <RM_Ismerrow>1</RM_Ismerrow>  <!-- ismerrow - no two plants alike -->
      <RM_Aphreen>2</RM_Aphreen>  <!-- aphreen - inflamed and perfectly healthy, most common bloom -->
      <RM_Nyssolet>1</RM_Nyssolet>  <!-- nyssolet - the jewel-like growth, attar fixative -->
      <RM_Sarrash>2</RM_Sarrash>  <!-- sarrash - the fever-crest plume -->
      <!-- the five predators (roster §5) - a separate clade, NOT bound by ban 2, eats scuttlers only -->
      <RM_Ullavess>2</RM_Ullavess>  <!-- ullavess - the standing pitcher -->
      <RM_Nemreth>1</RM_Nemreth>  <!-- nemreth - the jewelled sticky mat -->
      <RM_Velluric>1</RM_Velluric>  <!-- velluric - the trap is underwater -->
      <RM_Braskeen>1</RM_Braskeen>  <!-- braskeen - the only plant that moves -->
      <RM_Ommolyn>1</RM_Ommolyn>  <!-- ommolyn - the trap is buried -->
      <!-- the muck and the silt (roster §6) -->
      <RM_Immarel>2</RM_Immarel>  <!-- immarel - the attar's root-bed -->
      <RM_Thrannock>4</RM_Thrannock>  <!-- thrannock - the flotsam yard itself -->
      <RM_Pallasheen>1</RM_Pallasheen>  <!-- pallasheen - the loam prospector's tell -->
      <RM_Wessaline>1</RM_Wessaline>  <!-- wessaline - the salt-pan skin -->
      <RUT_Nogtyl MayRequire="mandrake.rut.rotsporekit">0.4</RUT_Nogtyl>  <!-- nogtyl - cross-mod, THEROT_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 owns updating this MayRequire -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>13</wildPlantRegrowDays>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
